{
  "summary": "This experiment tested the scgpt RNA encoder in a singleprofile setting, achieving validation accuracy of 0.4106 (F1: 0.3785), lower than the singleprofile baseline (pca_n2000) and multiprofile scvi_n200 models. The result suggests scgpt may underperform in singleprofile compared to other encoders, though its effectiveness relative to scvi_n200 and the impact of profile settings remain uncertain. Further comparison with aggregation methods or multimodal components is needed to isolate performance drivers."
}

